    "lawCode": "",
    "lawSection": "Real Property",
    "memo": " BILL NUMBER:  S3649\n\n TITLE OF BILL :\nAn act to authorize Bethel A.M.E. Church to file an application for\nreal property tax exemption\n\n\n PURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL :\nThis bill would authorize the Bethel A.M.E. Church to file an\napplication for a real property tax exemption.\n\n SUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS :\nSection 1 would authorize the Bethel A.M.E. Church 10 file an\napplication for a real property tax exemption for the 2007-08\nassessment rolls for the parcel owned by such not-for-profit\norganization which is located in Huntington Station at 51 10th Avenue.\n\n JUSTIFICATION :\nThe property located at 51 10th Avenue in Huntington Station has been\nowned by the Bethel A.M.E.  Church for many years. In the past, the\nparcel located at 51 10th Avenue was for non-church related purposes.\nHowever, since 2007, the property has been used for church-related\npurposes. The local municipality of the Town of Huntington has already\ngranted tax exempt status to Bethel AME for the year 2009. For the\nstated reasons Bethel A.M.E Church should be granted a real property\ntax exemption for the tax years 2007 and 2008.\n\n PRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY :\nNew bill.\n\n FISCAL IMPLICATIONS :\nNone to the State.\n\n EFFECTIVE DATE :\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
