    "lawCode": "",
    "lawSection": "Real Property",
    "memo": " BILL NUMBER:  S3649A\n\n TITLE OF BILL :\nAn act to authorize Bethel A.M.E. Church to file an application for\nreal property tax exemption\n\n\n PURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL :\nThis bill would authorize the Bethel AM.E. Church to file an\napplication for a real property tax exemption.\n\n SUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS :\nSection 1 would authorize the Bethel AM.E. Church to file an\napplication for a real property tax exemption for the 2006-2007, and\n2007-08 assessment rolls for the parcel owned by such not-for-profit\norganization which is located in Huntington Station at 51 10th Avenue.\n\n JUSTIFICATION :\nThe property located at 51 10th Avenue in Huntington Station has been\nowned by the Bethel A.M.E.  Church for many years. In the past, the\nparcel located at 51 10th Avenue was leased to other individuals for\nnon-church related purposes. However, since 2007, the property located\nat 51 10th Avenue in Huntington Station has been used for religious\npurposes. The local municipality of the Town of Huntington Station has\nalready granted tax exempt status to Bethel AME for the year 2009. For\nthe stated reasons Bethel A.M.E Church should be granted a real\nproperty tax exemption.\n\n PRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY :\nNew bill.\n\n FISCAL IMPLICATIONS :\nNone to the State.\n\n EFFECTIVE DATE :\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
